Requirements:
- add js file (link to html)
- file initiates the starting view and prompt the user to play a game
- use global variables (number of rounds, game score)
- add event handler to handle when dice is clicked
- use array for current roll of dice and global array to accumulate rolls for overall game
- functions used for processing a roll, updating html display, and game over

Parts:
code to roll dice (values, images)
code to process roll to determine score
code to update display and game state


- 1 is 100 points
- 5 is 50 points
- if you get three of the same it is 100x the number (exception: three 1s is 1000)
- 6 1s is an automatic win
- a roll can consist of the above rules (Example: 4 1s is 1100)

- dice will "roll" when the visitor clicks and stops after 1 second
- roll is new random number (from 1-6) every 100ms for each die
    (each photo needs to be associated to the correct die)
- user cannot restart the roll once it has started (has to wait until it is finished)
- pRolled heading displays the result of the roll
- pRollScore adds to the game score (displayed in hScore)
- tblRolls displays the roll list with most recent listed first
- add number of rolls required at the end of the game to roundList Header
